# Ref tactics compute

Import RefExample from "./ref_example.lg".

The tactics that compute, rewrite and decide. Every document here is checked by
the kernel in `factory selftest --live`.

## To exampleRfl () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`rfl` closes `Eq A x y` when `x` and `y` compute to the same value; `Nat_add` recurses on its SECOND argument, so `Nat_add n Zero` computes to `n`:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem two_plus_two : Eq Nat (Nat_add (Succ (Succ Zero)) (Succ (Succ Zero))) (Succ (Succ (Succ (Succ Zero))))" to doc.
    Push "  := by rfl." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Theorem add_zero_right : forall (n : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add n Zero) n := by intro n; rfl." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("rfl", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleInduction () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`induction n as [ | k ih]` leaves the `Zero` case, then the `Succ k` case with `ih`; `change` restates a goal as something it computes to, and `rw [h]` rewrites by an equation:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem zero_add : forall (n : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add Zero n) n := by intro n; induction n as [ | k ih]; rfl;" to doc.
    Push "  change Eq Nat (Succ (Nat_add Zero k)) (Succ k); rw [ih]; rfl." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("induction", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleRwReverse () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`rw [<- h]` rewrites right to left:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem rewrite_back : forall (a : Nat), forall (b : Nat), Eq Nat a b -> Eq Nat (Succ b) (Succ a) := by intro" to doc.
    Push "  a b h; rw [<- h]; rfl." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("rw_reverse", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleSubst () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`subst h` replaces a variable by what `h` equates it with:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem sym_by_subst : forall (a : Nat), forall (b : Nat), Eq Nat a b -> Eq Nat b a := by intro a b h; subst" to doc.
    Push "  h; rfl." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("subst", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleInjection () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`injection h as [e]` takes `Succ a = Succ b` to `a = b`:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem succ_inj_example : forall (a : Nat), forall (b : Nat), Eq Nat (Succ a) (Succ b) -> Eq Nat a b := by" to doc.
    Push "  intro a b h; injection h as [e]; exact e." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("injection", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleCasesImpossible () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`cases h` on an impossible equation or predicate closes the goal — no constructor can have built it:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem succ_ne_zero : forall (n : Nat), Not (Eq Nat (Succ n) Zero) := by intro n h; cases h." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Inductive Even : Nat -> Prop := even_zero : Even Zero | even_ss : forall (n : Nat), Even n -> Even (Succ (Succ" to doc.
    Push "  n))." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Theorem one_not_even : Not (Even (Succ Zero)) := by intro h; cases h." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("cases_impossible", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleDecide () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`decide` settles a closed decidable proposition by computing — equalities, `Not`, `Nat_le`, `Nat_lt` on numbers:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem two_ne_one : Not (Eq Nat (Succ (Succ Zero)) (Succ Zero)) := by decide." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Theorem one_le_two : Nat_le (Succ Zero) (Succ (Succ Zero)) := by decide." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("decide", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleCalc () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`calc [Eq A a b := p, Eq A _ c := q]` chains equations; `_` is the end of the step before:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem trans3 : forall (a : Nat), forall (b : Nat), forall (c : Nat), Eq Nat a b -> Eq Nat b c -> Eq Nat a c" to doc.
    Push "  := by intro a b c h1 h2; calc [Eq Nat a b := h1, Eq Nat _ c := h2]." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("calc", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleCc () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`cc` closes an equation the hypotheses give by congruence:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Axiom f : Nat -> Nat." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Theorem congr_example : forall (a : Nat), forall (b : Nat), Eq Nat a b -> Eq Nat (f a) (f b) := by intro a b" to doc.
    Push "  h; cc." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("cc", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleSimp () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`simp [l1, l2]` rewrites by the named equations until none applies, then closes the goal by `rfl`:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem plus_zero : forall (n : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add n Zero) n := by intro n; rfl." to doc.
    Push "" to doc.
    Push "Theorem simp_example : forall (a : Nat), Eq Nat (Nat_add (Nat_add a Zero) Zero) a := by intro a; simp" to doc.
    Push "  [plus_zero]." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("simp", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleRefine () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "`refine t` uses a term with `_` holes; each hole becomes a goal:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem pair_up : forall (P : Prop), forall (Q : Prop), P -> Q -> And P Q := by intro P Q p q; refine (conj P" to doc.
    Push "  Q _ _); exact p; exact q." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("refine", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## To exampleIntLaws () -> RefExample:
    Let lead be "The integer laws are theorems to cite: `add_comm`, `add_assoc`, `mul_comm`, `mul_assoc`, `mul_distrib_add`, `add_zero`, `mul_one`, `le_refl`, `le_trans`:".
    Let mutable doc be a new Seq of Text.
    Push "Theorem int_add_comm_example : forall (a : Int), forall (b : Int), Eq Int (add a b) (add b a) := by intro a b;" to doc.
    Push "  exact (add_comm a b)." to doc.
    Return positiveExample("int_laws", lead, join(doc, "\n")).

## Note
This file's examples, in the order the reference shows them.

## To computeTacticExamples () -> Seq of RefExample:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of RefExample.
    Push exampleRfl() to out.
    Push exampleInduction() to out.
    Push exampleRwReverse() to out.
    Push exampleSubst() to out.
    Push exampleInjection() to out.
    Push exampleCasesImpossible() to out.
    Push exampleDecide() to out.
    Push exampleCalc() to out.
    Push exampleCc() to out.
    Push exampleSimp() to out.
    Push exampleRefine() to out.
    Push exampleIntLaws() to out.
    Return out.
